<title>LEBANON: Lebanon's Fransabank profits up 57 pct.</title>
<headline>Lebanon's Fransabank profits up 57 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's Fransabank reported on Tuesday a 57 percent rise in net profits in 1996 to 42.1 billion Lebanese pounds ($27.1 million) from 26.78 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>It said its ranking in terms of net profits rose to third in 1996 from fourth in 1995 among Lebanon's 82 banks.</p>
<p>It ranked fifth in customer deposits and sixth in assets among Lebanon's 82 banks in 1996, the bank said.</p>
<p>Fransabank issued the following results (in billions of Lebanese pounds unless otherwise stated. Change on previous year in brackets):</p>
<p>			     1996		     1995     % change</p>
<p>    Net profits	    42.10		   26.78     (57)</p>
<p>    Assets		2,174.60		1,733.53     (25.44)</p>
<p>    Deposits	    1,829.40		1,456.78     (25.58)</p>
<p>    Loans		   558.07		  453.32     (23.11)</p>
<p>Shareholder</p>
<p>    Equity		  123.25		   77.80     (59.70)</p>
<p>Other details</p>
<p>    Return on assets (%)  2.15		    1.71</p>
<p>Return on equity (%) 73.87</p>
<p>    Solvency ratio   (%) 20.40</p>
<p>$1 = 1,552 Lebanese pounds at 31/12/1996</p>
<p>$1 = 1,596 Lebanese pounds at 31/12/1995</p>
<p>-- Beirut editorial (9611)  745307  745308  602057</p>
